{"fileVersion":"1.0","metadata":{"title":"Baron Coleman","description":"A sourced public-figure graph about attorney, political consultant, former radio host, and Real Baron Podcast host George Baron Coleman.","graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph","version":"0.3.0","kind":"person","created":"2026-08-07T17:10:00.000Z","modified":"2026-08-07T18:18:00.000Z","author":"","tags":["person","public","lionel-v1","sourced-profile","attorney","podcast","politics"],"preferredViewer":"https://twilite.zone"},"nodes":[{"id":"baron-coleman-declaration","type":"declaration","label":"Baron Coleman Declaration","position":{"x":-1500,"y":-1050},"width":440,"height":320,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":false,"showLabel":true,"data":{"analytics":{"contentGroup":"people"},"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph","name":"Baron Coleman","version":"0.3.0","description":"A sourced public-figure graph about attorney, political consultant, former radio host, and Real Baron Podcast host George Baron Coleman.","createdAt":"2026-08-07T17:10:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T18:18:00.000Z"},"intent":{"kind":"person","scope":"public"},"dependencies":{"nodeTypes":["declaration","bridge","port","person","markdown"],"portContracts":["core"],"schemaVersions":{"nodes":">=1.0.0","ports":">=1.0.0"}},"authority":{"mode":"graph","mutation":{"allowCreate":true,"allowUpdate":true,"allowDelete":true,"appendOnly":false},"actors":{"humans":true,"agents":true,"tools":true},"history":{"rewriteAllowed":false,"squashAllowed":false}},"declaration":{"kind":"person","targetMode":"artifact","artifactKind":"graph","defaultSurfaceId":"root","surfaces":[{"id":"root","kind":"port","label":"Baron Coleman","portNodeId":"baron-coleman-detail","viewNodeId":"baron-coleman-detail"},{"id":"baron-coleman-icon-surface","kind":"view","label":"Icon","viewNodeId":"baron-coleman-icon-surface"}]}}},{"id":"baron-coleman-person-bridge","type":"bridge","label":"Person","position":{"x":-1500,"y":-680},"width":260,"height":100,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"visible":false,"showLabel":true,"data":{"authority":"bridge","target":{"mode":"bridge","ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node","kind":"node-class","resourceKind":"node-class","scope":"focused-graph","grants":["create"],"key":"person","label":"Person"},"resourceKind":"node-class","scope":"focused-graph","grants":["create"],"bridge":{"ref":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node","resourceKind":"node-class","scope":"focused-graph","grants":["create"]},"_classBinding":{"key":"person","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node"},"_bridge":{"sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node","entryPort":"root","kind":"node-class","targetKind":"node-class","classKey":"person","classRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node"}}},{"id":"baron-coleman-detail","type":"port","label":"Baron Coleman","position":{"x":-380,"y":-1080},"width":800,"height":600,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph","portId":"root","name":"Baron Coleman"},"view":{"intent":"node","payload":"node.web.summary","label":"Baron Coleman"},"renderShape":{"kind":"markdown"},"markdown":"# 👤 Baron Coleman\n\n![Portrait of Baron Coleman](https://image-cdn-ak.spotifycdn.com/image/ab6772ab00001692835251c375c695f38503e18c)\n\n**George Baron Coleman**  \n**attorney · political consultant · former radio host · podcast host**\n\nAmerican lawyer and political-media figure with roughly two decades in legal practice. Coleman founded **Baron Coleman Law Firm**, has worked in criminal defense, appeals and civil litigation, and has a documented history in Alabama politics and political consulting. Since late 2025 he has become much more visible nationally through the **Real Baron Podcast** and his commentary on the Charlie Kirk case and related political controversies.\n\n### At a glance\n- **Education:** Faulkner University, B.S. (2002); Indiana University School of Law, J.D. (2006)\n- **Admissions listed:** Alabama (2006), Florida (2007), Tennessee (2023)\n- **Florida status:** member in good standing; no discipline listed in the Florida Bar's 10-year history\n- **Firm:** Baron Coleman Law Firm\n- **Media:** former WACV *News and Views* host; host of *Real Baron Podcast*\n- **Political work:** polling, campaign management, messaging, grassroots organization and earlier registered lobbying work\n\n*Profile refreshed from professional directories, bar records, court/reporting sources and current media listings on 7 Aug 2026.*"}},{"id":"baron-coleman-icon-surface","type":"port","label":"Baron Coleman Icon","position":{"x":500,"y":-1010},"width":250,"height":220,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph","portId":"baron-coleman-icon-surface","name":"Baron Coleman Icon"},"portrait":"https://image-cdn-ak.spotifycdn.com/image/ab6772ab00001692835251c375c695f38503e18c","displayName":"Baron Coleman","view":{"intent":"graph","payload":"graph.web.icon","label":"Icon"},"renderShape":{"kind":"html"},"html":"<div style=\"width:100%;height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:16px;border-radius:24px;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#fff8dc,#fef3c7);border:3px solid #f59e0b;color:#111827;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:10px;font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;overflow:hidden\"><div style=\"width:118px;height:118px;padding:5px;border-radius:999px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fbbf24,#b45309);box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(146,64,14,.28)\"><img src=\"{{data.portrait}}\" alt=\"Portrait of {{data.displayName}}\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 20%;border-radius:999px;background:#fde68a\"/></div><div style=\"width:100%;font-size:17px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:850;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis\">{{data.displayName}}</div></div>","payload":"graph.web.icon","intent":"graph","key":"graph.web.icon","viewRole":"icon","viewKind":"display","semanticLevel":"icon","visibilityRole":"editor","memo":"Compact portrait-and-name surface for Baron Coleman."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-person","type":"person","label":"Baron Coleman","position":{"x":-120,"y":-360},"width":540,"height":380,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90},{"id":"left","label":"left","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":180}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"displayName":"Baron Coleman","fullName":"George Baron Coleman","aliases":["George Baron Coleman"],"summary":"American attorney, political consultant, former Alabama radio host, and host of the Real Baron Podcast. Coleman founded Baron Coleman Law Firm and has practiced criminal defense, appellate and civil litigation while also working in political consulting and commentary.","portrait":"https://image-cdn-ak.spotifycdn.com/image/ab6772ab00001692835251c375c695f38503e18c","birthDate":"","deathDate":"","pronouns":"","nationality":"American","primaryRoles":["attorney","criminal defense lawyer","appellate lawyer","political consultant","former radio host","podcast host","political commentator"],"canonicalUri":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/baron-coleman.node","status":"published","definitionKey":"person","_classBinding":{"key":"person","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node"},"_bridge":{"classKey":"person","classRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node","entryPort":"root","kind":"node-class","sourceRef":"github://mikemartinez1974/public/people/template/person.node-class.node","targetKind":"node-class"}}},{"id":"baron-coleman-quick-answers","type":"markdown","label":"Quick Answers","position":{"x":-1260,"y":180},"width":720,"height":560,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🧭 Quick answers\n\n**Who is he?**  \nGeorge Baron Coleman is a lawyer who has also spent years around political consulting, lobbying and talk radio. His current national profile comes mainly from the *Real Baron Podcast*.\n\n**Did he just appear out of nowhere?**  \nNo. Public records put him in Alabama legal and political circles for well over a decade. He was a registered lobbyist in Alabama in the early 2010s, later hosted *News and Views* on WACV in Montgomery, and publicly weighed entering Republican electoral politics in 2019.\n\n**Where is he based now?**  \nOlder firm directories still identify Montgomery, Alabama. The Florida Bar currently lists his firm's mailing address in **Spring Hill, Tennessee**, and a Tennessee attorney listing records his 2023 admission there.\n\n**How long has he practiced law?**  \nSince 2006, according to attorney directories and bar records.\n\n**How old is he? Is he married? How many children?**  \nI did not find a sufficiently strong primary or professional source for his birth date or detailed family biography. Fan communities and low-authority biography sites repeat claims that he is married and has eight children, but this graph does **not** promote those claims to established biographical facts without better sourcing."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-legal-career","type":"markdown","label":"Legal Career","position":{"x":-470,"y":180},"width":720,"height":560,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## ⚖️ Legal career\n\nColeman earned a **B.S. from Faulkner University in 2002** and a **J.D. from Indiana University School of Law in 2006**. Attorney profiles list early associate positions at Webster Henry Lyons & White (2006–2008) and Sasser Sefton Connally Tipton & Davis (2008–2009), followed by founding **Baron Coleman Law Firm** in 2009.\n\nHis profiles emphasize **criminal defense and appeals**, while broader directories also list civil litigation, trial work, insurance defense and medical-malpractice defense. Avvo says he has tried criminal matters in state and federal courts across several states and lists a military-law peer endorsement describing his work on court-martial defense teams.\n\nAvvo also lists him as the **2012 Volunteer Lawyer of the Year** from the Montgomery County Bar Association and records speaking engagements and a 2010 tax-policy publication. Those details are directory/profile claims rather than independent evaluations of his skill."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-licenses","type":"markdown","label":"Licenses and Standing","position":{"x":320,"y":180},"width":720,"height":560,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 📜 Licenses and professional standing\n\nProfessional directories list these admissions:\n\n- **Alabama:** 2006\n- **Florida:** 2007\n- **Tennessee:** 2023\n- Federal courts in Alabama and northern Florida, plus the **U.S. Court of Appeals for the Eleventh Circuit**\n\nThe **Florida Bar** currently lists George Baron Coleman as a **member in good standing**, eligible to practice in Florida, with **no discipline in its displayed 10-year history**. It identifies Baron Coleman Law Firm as a one-lawyer firm and gives a Spring Hill, Tennessee mailing address.\n\nAvvo currently marks his Alabama, Florida and Tennessee licenses as active/authorized and reports no misconduct found in its license summary. For any hiring decision, the state bar itself remains the authoritative place to verify current status."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-early-political-media","type":"markdown","label":"Political and Media Background","position":{"x":1110,"y":180},"width":720,"height":560,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🎙️ Political and media background before the podcast\n\nColeman's political-media career predates the *Real Baron Podcast* by years. Alabama ethics archives list **George Baron Coleman as a registered lobbyist** in the early 2010s; entries include Coleman Kennamer LLC and, in 2013, the Alabama Brewers Guild.\n\nHis LinkedIn profile describes work through **ONE R, LLC** offering political services including **polling, campaign management, messaging and grassroots creation/organization**. It also lists service on the finance council of Holy Spirit Catholic Church from 2011–2021 and past board involvement with C.O.P.E. of Montgomery.\n\nBy 2019 Alabama Today described Coleman as a **lawyer, radio talk-show host and political consultant** whose weekday *News and Views* program aired on WACV 93.1 FM in Montgomery. During the state gas-tax fight he publicly threatened to challenge Republican state representative Reed Ingram if Ingram voted for the tax.\n\nSo the podcast is a new national chapter, not the beginning of his political commentary career."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-notable-representations","type":"markdown","label":"Notable Representations","position":{"x":-1260,"y":820},"width":720,"height":600,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🏛️ Notable representations and politically charged work\n\nColeman's legal practice has included clients and cases embedded in contentious political disputes.\n\n- In **2019**, Coleman was lead counsel for **Gavin McInnes**, founder of the Proud Boys, in a defamation suit against the Southern Poverty Law Center over its hate-group designation. A 2025 federal opinion in the case still lists George Baron Coleman among McInnes's attorneys. Representation of a client does not by itself establish an attorney's personal agreement with that client's politics.\n- In **2020**, reporting based on Alabama state records said Coleman registered **Stop the Steal LLC** in Montgomery. Ali Alexander told SPLC Hatewatch that Coleman represented him.\n- In Alexander's **December 2021 deposition** before the House January 6 committee, Alexander identified Baron Coleman as one of his legal counsel, noting Coleman was not present that day.\n\nA 2021 Alabama Political Reporter correction is worth preserving: a Capitol Police lawsuit named **Ali Alexander and Stop the Steal LLC**, care of Coleman, but **Coleman himself was not a defendant** in that suit."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-alabama-history","type":"markdown","label":"Alabama Political History","position":{"x":-470,"y":820},"width":720,"height":600,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🧩 A less obvious chapter: Alabama political investigations\n\nColeman's earlier political history is not a simple partisan résumé. In 2016, **Alabama Political Reporter** wrote that court filings identified Coleman as having served as a **confidential informant for the Alabama Attorney General's Special Prosecution Division** beginning in 2012. The report said he supplied information involving then-House Speaker Mike Hubbard and others.\n\nThe same reporting described a later twist: Coleman gave an affidavit to **Hubbard's defense lawyers**, who used it to renew claims of prosecutorial misconduct.\n\nThis episode matters because it shows Coleman operating simultaneously in legal, investigative, media and political worlds years before his current podcast fame. The underlying court material included sealed evidence, so this graph states only what the cited public reporting says and does not infer motives beyond it."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-podcast","type":"markdown","label":"Real Baron Podcast","position":{"x":320,"y":820},"width":720,"height":600,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🎧 Real Baron Podcast\n\nThe **Real Baron Podcast** is Coleman's current media vehicle. Apple Podcasts identifies **Baron Coleman** as creator and describes the show with the tagline **“Intellectually Honest. Philosophically Consistent.”** The show combines long-form legal reasoning, politics, evidence review, audience interaction and live commentary.\n\nBy August 2026 Apple Podcasts listed roughly **148 episodes**, reflecting a very high publishing cadence. Current episodes run several hours and frequently separate an opening analytical monologue from later audience questions and paid-message discussion.\n\nColeman's public X bio likewise identifies him as host of the Real Baron Podcast and associates the content with **ONE R, LLC**. His X account, created in October 2025, grew to well over 100,000 followers by mid-2026. Because follower and episode counts move quickly, those numbers should be read as an **August 2026 snapshot**, not permanent metadata."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-candace","type":"markdown","label":"Candace Owens and Recent Visibility","position":{"x":1110,"y":820},"width":720,"height":600,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0},{"id":"bottom","label":"bottom","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":90}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 📡 Candace Owens and the recent visibility surge\n\nColeman's national visibility increased sharply in **late 2025 and 2026** as he devoted extensive podcast coverage to the killing of Charlie Kirk, the prosecution of Tyler Robinson, TPUSA figures, Candace Owens's reporting and competing theories circulating around the case.\n\nOn **20 January 2026**, Owens hosted a long-form episode titled *Candace x Baron Coleman LIVE!!* in which Coleman joined her for discussion of TPUSA personnel, military connections, media claims and Charlie Kirk-related questions. The episode drew a very large audience on Owens's channel.\n\nColeman's own programs frequently analyze material raised by Owens and other independent commentators, but his show is not merely a Candace recap channel: he adds legal/proof analysis, source comparison, historical/political context and long audience sessions.\n\n**Attribution boundary:** many claims discussed in this media ecosystem are disputed, speculative or unproven. This profile documents Coleman's role and public activity; it does not treat his theories, Owens's theories, or their critics' theories as established facts."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-personal-known-unknown","type":"markdown","label":"Personal Details: Known and Unknown","position":{"x":-860,"y":1500},"width":760,"height":520,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🔎 Personal details: what is actually well sourced?\n\nColeman is much easier to source professionally than biographically.\n\n### Strongly supported\n- Full professional name: **George Baron Coleman**\n- Education and bar admissions\n- Long association with Montgomery, Alabama legal and political circles\n- Current Florida Bar mailing address in Spring Hill, Tennessee\n- LinkedIn lists a decade on the **Holy Spirit Catholic Church Finance Council**\n\n### Widely repeated but not promoted here as verified fact\nOnline fan communities and lightweight biography sites repeatedly say Coleman is married and has **eight children**, and some name his spouse. Those sources are not strong enough for this graph to convert private-family details into authoritative biography.\n\n### Not established in the sources used here\n- exact birth date / age\n- detailed childhood or family history\n\nThis card is intentionally explicit so a reader can tell the difference between **missing information** and **information we chose not to overstate**."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-lionel-context","type":"markdown","label":"Lionel Episode Context","position":{"x":-20,"y":1500},"width":760,"height":520,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🎙️ Lionel episode context\n\nIn **Lionel Template v1 Example 01**, Coleman appears both as a named actor and as a contributor in the **Research Funnel**. That placement reflects Lionel's description of a distributed research/commentary network around Candace Owens, Robert Barnes and other independent media figures.\n\nThe richer biography helps explain why Coleman is useful to Lionel's argument: he is not simply another online commentator. He brings a combination of **trial-law experience, Alabama political history, campaign/political consulting and long-form media work**.\n\nThe Lionel graph records Lionel's interpretation of Coleman's role in the information network. This person graph supplies durable identity and career context without independently validating the investigative claims discussed in that episode.\n\n**Lionel example:** `github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/lionel/v1/example-01-associative-realignment.node`"}},{"id":"baron-coleman-sources-professional","type":"markdown","label":"Professional Sources","position":{"x":820,"y":1500},"width":900,"height":620,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 📚 Professional and biographical sources\n\n- **The Florida Bar**, George Baron Coleman “Baron” member profile  \n  https://www.floridabar.org/directories/find-mbr/profile/?num=35489\n- **Avvo**, George Baron Coleman profile  \n  https://www.avvo.com/attorneys/george-coleman-1237726.html\n- **Lawyers.com / Martindale-Avvo**, Mr. George Baron Coleman  \n  https://www.lawyers.com/montgomery/alabama/george-coleman-35435903-a/\n- **Martindale**, George Baron Coleman profile  \n  https://www.martindale.com/attorney/george-baron-coleman-35435903/\n- **LinkedIn**, Baron Coleman — ONE R, LLC  \n  https://www.linkedin.com/in/baroncoleman\n- **Alabama Ethics Commission**, archived lobbyist lists (2012–2014)  \n  https://ethics.alabama.gov/docs/lobbylist/2013_Lobb_List_Arch_12_31_13.pdf\n\n### Photo provenance\nPortrait currently uses Real Baron Podcast artwork distributed by Spotify.\n\n**Portrait URL:** https://image-cdn-ak.spotifycdn.com/image/ab6772ab00001692835251c375c695f38503e18c"}},{"id":"baron-coleman-sources-history","type":"markdown","label":"Political and Legal History Sources","position":{"x":-480,"y":2160},"width":960,"height":650,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 🧾 Political and legal-history sources\n\n- **Alabama Today**, *Baron Coleman doubles down against gas tax, promises to run against Reed Ingram*  \n  https://altoday.com/archives/tag/baron-coleman\n- **Alabama Political Reporter**, *Coleman Revealed as Confidential Informant, Gave Affidavit to Mike Hubbard* (2016)  \n  https://www.alreporter.com/2016/02/12/coleman-revealed-as-confidential-informant-gave-affidavit-to-mike-hubbard/\n- **Southern Poverty Law Center / Hatewatch**, report on Stop the Steal LLC registration (2020)  \n  https://www.splcenter.org/resources/hatewatch/law-firm-tied-far-right-fringe-registers-stop-steal-llc-alabama/\n- **Alabama Political Reporter**, correction and context on Capitol Police suit (2021)  \n  https://www.alreporter.com/2021/10/26/far-right-activist-and-his-alabama-attorney-sued-by-u-s-capitol-police/\n- **Ali Alexander deposition**, House January 6 Select Committee, 9 Dec 2021  \n  https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/CTRL0000034607_-_Deposition_of_Ali_Alexander%2C_%28Dec._9%2C_2021%29.pdf\n- **Courthouse News Service**, McInnes defamation case background  \n  https://www.courthousenews.com/proud-boys-founder-sues-over-hate-group-label/\n- **2025 federal opinion**, McInnes v. SPLC, listing counsel  \n  https://www.leagle.com/decision/infdco20251023953\n\n**Source note:** SPLC was itself the defendant in McInnes's case, so its reporting is used for specific documented facts and cross-checked where possible rather than treated as a neutral characterization of the litigation."}},{"id":"baron-coleman-sources-media","type":"markdown","label":"Media Sources","position":{"x":540,"y":2160},"width":900,"height":650,"ports":[{"id":"root","label":"root","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"any","angle":210},{"id":"top","label":"top","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":270},{"id":"right","label":"right","direction":"bidirectional","dataType":"value","angle":0}],"visible":true,"showLabel":false,"data":{"identity":{"graphId":"baron-coleman-person-graph"},"markdown":"## 📺 Current media sources\n\n- **Apple Podcasts**, *Real Baron Podcast*  \n  https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/real-baron-podcast/id1865794721\n- **Spotify**, *Real Baron Podcast*  \n  https://open.spotify.com/show/7gGJDxfhTfMnZawXVbsO1C\n- **X**, Baron Coleman / @baroncoleman  \n  https://x.com/baroncoleman\n- **Candace Owens / YouTube**, *Candace x Baron Coleman LIVE!! | Candace Ep 293* (20 Jan 2026)  \n  https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9naMwS0kMBE\n- **Baron Coleman / YouTube**, example long-form program from Nov 2025  \n  https://www.youtube.com/live/ZBZdTiikAX8\n\n### Research posture\nCurrent-show material is used to document **what Coleman publishes and how his public role has developed**. Claims made inside those programs are not converted into biography facts unless independently sourced."}}],"edges":[{"id":"baron-coleman-class","source":"baron-coleman-declaration","target":"baron-coleman-person-bridge","source